5️⃣ TYPES OF DEPENDENCY INJECTION (DI)
    -> Field injection(not recommended)     ------>Spring injects dependency directly into the variable
🔹 Example:
   @RestController
   public class UserController {

      @Autowired
      private UserService userService;

      @GetMapping("/msg")
      public String msg() {
          return userService.message();
      }
  }

    -> Constructor injection(recommended)   ------>Spring injects dependency directly into the constructor
  🔹Example
     @RestController
     public class UserController {
     private final UserService userService;
     public UserController(UserService userService){
          this.userService=userService
      }
      @GetMapping("/msg")
      public String msg() {
          return userService.message();
      }
  }

 -> Setter injection(rarely used)        ------>Spring injects dependency directly into the setter method
 🔹Example
   @Service
   public class UserService {
   private MessageService messageService;
     @Autowired
     public void setMessageService(MessageService messageService) {
          this.messageService = messageService;
     }
  }
