1️⃣ Create a Bean
import jakarta.annotation.PostConstruct;
import jakarta.annotation.PreDestroy;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
@Component
public class LifeCycleBean {
    public LifeCycleBean() {
        System.out.println("1️⃣ Bean Constructor Called");
    }

    @PostConstruct
    public void init() {
        System.out.println("3️⃣ @PostConstruct: Bean Initialized");
    }

    @PreDestroy
    public void destroy() {
        System.out.println("6️⃣ @PreDestroy: Bean Destroyed");
    }
}

2️⃣ Use the Bean in Controller
@RestController
public class TestController {
    private final LifeCycleBean lifeCycleBean;
    public TestController(LifeCycleBean lifeCycleBean) {
        this.lifeCycleBean = lifeCycleBean;
    }

    @GetMapping("/test")
    public String test() {
        return "Bean is ready and working";
    }
}

🔵 WHAT HAPPENS INTERNALLY (VERY IMPORTANT)
🟢 When Application STARTS
1️⃣ Bean Constructor Called
3️⃣ @PostConstruct: Bean Initialized

➡ Bean is now ready to use

🟢 When API is CALLED
GET /test

Response:
Bean is ready and working
➡ Bean is already created, so Spring just uses it

🔴 When Application STOPS
6️⃣ @PreDestroy: Bean Destroyed

➡ Bean cleanup happens
