LEVEL 4 – DATABASE + JPA (SPRING DATA JPA)
1️⃣ Spring Data JPA
    What is it?
    Spring data jpa is a spring module which lets you to handle db operations easily,without writing sql again and again
    
    why we use it?
      -> To avoid JDBC boilerplate code.
      -> To avoid writing sql query for basic CRUD operations.
      -> Uses Repository interface

    Example:
    public interface Repository extends JpaRepository<User,Integer>{}

    with this one line you get:-
      -> Save
      -> findById()
      -> findByAll()
      -> deleteById()

2️⃣ ORM Basics (Object Relational Mapping)
    What is ORM?
      ORM(Object Relational Mapping) is used to map java objects with database tables.

    Simple meaning:
      Java classes <> database table
      Java objects <> table rows
      fields <> columns
    Example:
      User user = new User(1,"Sujan","sujan2002@gmail.com")

    Automatically stored as:
     _______________________________________________________________________
     |id                      |   name                | email              |
     -----------------------------------------------------------------------
     |1                       |   Sujan               | sujan2002@gmail.com|
     |_____________________________________________________________________|

3️⃣ Entity Mapping
    What is an Entity?
      Entity is used to map java classes with database table    

    Key Annotations:
      @Entity: marks the class as table
      @Id: primary key
      @GeneratedValue: auto id

    Example:
    @Entity
    public class User{
        @Id
        @GeneratedValue
        private int id;
        private String name;
        private String email;
    }

📌 Spring automatically creates table:
    User(id,name,email) 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4️⃣ Repositories
    What is Repository?
     Repository is used to handle DB operations

    Why interface?
     Spring automatically creates the implementation at runtime

    Example:
    public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User,Integer>{}

    Advasntages:
     ->no need for SQL code
     ->no need for implementation class
     ->Direct DB access
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5️⃣ CRUD using JpaRepository
    CRUD Meaning 
      -> CREATE
      -> READ
      -> UPDATE
      -> DELETE

    Example:
      repository.save(user)    ----->create/update/insert
      repository.findAll()     ----->read
      repository.findById(1)   ----->read by id
      repository.deleteById()  ----->delete
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6️⃣ Find by Name / Email – Derived Queries
❓ What is this?
    Spring data JPA automatically creates SQL Queries based on the method name in user repository.

    Example:
    public interface UserRepository extends Jparepository{
       List<User> findByName(String name);
       User findByEmail(String email);
    }
